<title>USA: Lockheed Martin gets defense contract rise. [CORRECTED 22:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin gets defense contract rise. [CORRECTED 22:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Corp has received a total $462.3 million increase to two contracts to provide C-130J aircraft to the Air Force, the Department of Defense said Tuesday.</p>
<p>A contract to provide six aircraft was increased by $273.9 million, while another contract, to provide four aircraft, was increased by $188.4 million.</p>
<p>Both contracts are expected to be completed in December 1998.</p>
<p>(Corrects total figure and number of contracts).</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
